IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sssa-nouns`
IMPORT `sssa-part1-preliminary`

-- Silver Support Scheme Act 2015 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation in force from 1 December 2025 -- LAYER 1, PART 3: ADMINISTRATION.
--
-- ss 8 and 9 let the Minister direct a department to hand over information and
-- limit what then may be done with it; s 10 makes overpaid and fraudulently
-- obtained sums recoverable.  What a "benefit", a "criterion" or a "public scheme"
-- is, and who is "prescribed", is left to regulations that are not among the
-- sources, so each such fact is an INPUT.
--
-- Two shapes appear for a duty or a bar.  A regulative rule (PARTY ... MUST or
-- SHANT ...) is run with #TRACE, whose outcome prints and cannot be asserted on
-- the stable binary; each is therefore paired with a decision function that
-- answers the same question over plain facts, and the assertions are made on that
-- function.  Every duty here has no time limit in the text, so none is invented.

§ `Silver Support Scheme Act 2015 -- Part 3 -- Administration`

§§ `The ceiling of a penalty`

-- Every offence in the Act is written "a fine not exceeding $x or ... imprisonment
-- for a term not exceeding n months or ... both".  This function checks a proposed
-- sentence against such a ceiling.  It is arithmetic, not a section; the wording is
-- quoted once here, at s 8(6), and each section's own ceiling is cited at its constant.
-- src:400 | (6) Any person who does any act in contravention of subsection (3)
-- src:401 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:402 | not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:403 | 12 months or to both.
@ref SSSA2015 the form of a ceiling in ss 8(6), 9(7), 11(1), 14(4), 15 and 20(3) (src:400-403)
GIVEN pen IS A Penalty
      fine IS A NUMBER
      months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a sentence is within the ceiling of a penalty` MEANS
    fine AT MOST pen's `greatest fine in dollars` AND months AT MOST pen's `greatest imprisonment in months`

§§ `s 8 Provision of information for administration of Act or Scheme`

-- s 8(1)(a): the Minister may direct the department to provide "so much of the
-- means information as is necessary for that purpose".  The grant is conferred
-- "Where the Minister certifies in writing", and reaches only means information
-- that is necessary; a case outside those limits is not answered by the text.
-- src:298 | 8.—(1) Where the Minister certifies in writing that it is necessary
-- src:299 | for an authorised person to have access to any particular class of
-- src:300 | means information in the possession of a Government department or
-- src:305 | public authority, in order to facilitate the administration or
-- src:306 | enforcement of this Act or the administration of the Scheme —
-- src:308 | (a) the Minister charged with the responsibility for that
-- src:309 | Government department or public authority may, in
-- src:310 | addition to any other power conferred by any written
-- src:311 | law, direct that Government department or public authority
-- src:312 | to provide to the authorised person so much of the means
-- src:313 | information as is necessary for that purpose; and
@ref SSSA2015 s 8(1)(a) (src:298-313)
GIVEN `the Minister has certified in writing that it is necessary for an authorised person to have access to the class of means information, in order to facilitate the administration or enforcement of this Act or the administration of the Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is means information` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the information is necessary for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(1)(a) the Minister may direct the department or authority to provide the information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Minister has certified in writing that it is necessary for an authorised person to have access to the class of means information, in order to facilitate the administration or enforcement of this Act or the administration of the Scheme`
           AND `the information is means information` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `the information is necessary for that purpose`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power arises "Where the Minister certifies in writing" and reaches only "so much of the means information as is necessary for that purpose"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 8(1)(b): the department "is to comply with the direction", despite any other
-- written law and whether or not it is under an obligation not to disclose.  The
-- obligation not to disclose is no condition, so it is not an input.
-- src:315 | (b) that Government department or public authority is to
-- src:316 | comply with the direction under paragraph (a), despite any
-- src:317 | other written law, and whether or not it is under any
-- src:318 | obligation (imposed by written law or otherwise) not to
-- src:319 | disclose such information.
@ref SSSA2015 s 8(1)(b) (src:315-319)
GIVEN `a direction has been given under section 8(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(1)(b) the department or authority must comply with the direction` MEANS
    IF `a direction has been given under section 8(1)(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is "to comply with the direction under paragraph (a)" and says nothing where there is none
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The same duty as a regulative rule.  The text gives no time limit.
-- src:315 | (b) that Government department or public authority is to
-- src:316 | comply with the direction under paragraph (a), despite any
-- src:317 | other written law, and whether or not it is under any
-- src:318 | obligation (imposed by written law or otherwise) not to
-- src:319 | disclose such information.
@ref SSSA2015 s 8(1)(b) (src:315-319)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party under the Act` `An act under the Act`
`s 8(1)(b) duty of the department or authority` MEANS
    PARTY `the Government department or public authority`
    MUST `provide the information to the authorised person`

-- EXPECT FULFILLED: the department provides at time 3.
#TRACE `s 8(1)(b) duty of the department or authority` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Government department or public authority` DOES `provide the information to the authorised person` AT 3
-- EXPECT FULFILLED: the text gives no time limit, so a department that provides at time 300 has done what the subsection requires.
#TRACE `s 8(1)(b) duty of the department or authority` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Government department or public authority` DOES `provide the information to the authorised person` AT 300
-- EXPECT PENDING: nothing done by time 100; the duty is still outstanding (PARTY ... MUST ...), not a breach.
#TRACE `s 8(1)(b) duty of the department or authority` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

-- s 8(2)(a): the same power over confidential information other than means information, for an information recipient.
-- src:321 | (2) Where the Minister certifies in writing that it is necessary for an
-- src:322 | information recipient to have access to any particular class of
