      `the information is confidential information other than means information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is necessary for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(2)(a) the Minister may direct the department or authority to provide the information` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has certified in writing that it is necessary for an information recipient to have access to the class of confidential information, in order to facilitate the administration or enforcement of this Act or the administration of the Scheme`
       AND `the information is confidential information other than means information`
       AND `the information is necessary for that purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power arises "Where the Minister certifies in writing" and reaches only "so much of the confidential information as is necessary for that purpose"
    ELSE NOTHING

