-- s 8(3): an individual who has opted out.  "If an individual opts out" is a
-- condition (a failed "if" answers no, reading (a)); "from the time an authorised
-- person is notified" is a start time (a case before it falls outside the wording,
-- reading (b)); "except with the consent of that individual" answers no.  Only the
-- two acts the subsection names are barred; any other act is not spoken of.
-- src:342 | (3) If an individual opts out, in the manner determined by the
-- src:343 | Commissioner, from the application of subsection (1) to means
-- src:344 | information about the individual, then from the time an authorised
-- src:345 | person is notified that the individual has opted out, the authorised
-- src:346 | person must not —
-- src:351 | (a) access any means information about the individual
-- src:352 | obtained under that subsection; or
-- src:354 | (b) use or disclose under section 9 any such means information
-- src:355 | that the authorised person had previously accessed,
-- src:357 | except with the consent of that individual.
@ref SSSA2015 s 8(3) (src:342-357)
GIVEN act IS AN `Act on means information`
      `the individual has opted out, in the manner determined by the Commissioner, from the application of section 8(1) to means information about the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorised person has been notified that the individual has opted out` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(3) the authorised person is barred from the act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF act EQUALS `any other act`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the authorised person "must not" only "(a) access" or "(b) use or disclose under section 9"
        THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an individual opts out, in the manner determined by the Commissioner, from the application of subsection (1)"
        IF NOT `the individual has opted out, in the manner determined by the Commissioner, from the application of section 8(1) to means information about the individual` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except with the consent of that individual"
        IF `the individual has consented` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar runs "from the time an authorised person is notified that the individual has opted out"
        IF NOT `the authorised person has been notified that the individual has opted out` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The same bar as a regulative rule: access.  The bar runs from notification and has no end in the text.
-- src:342 | (3) If an individual opts out, in the manner determined by the
-- src:343 | Commissioner, from the application of subsection (1) to means
-- src:344 | information about the individual, then from the time an authorised
-- src:345 | person is notified that the individual has opted out, the authorised
-- src:346 | person must not —
-- src:351 | (a) access any means information about the individual
-- src:352 | obtained under that subsection; or
-- src:357 | except with the consent of that individual.
@ref SSSA2015 s 8(3)(a) (src:342-357)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party under the Act` `An act under the Act`
`s 8(3)(a) bar on the authorised person` MEANS
    PARTY `the authorised person`
    SHANT `access the means information`
    LEST BREACH BY `the authorised person` BECAUSE "the authorised person accessed means information after being notified that the individual opted out, and without the individual's consent"

-- The same bar: use or disclosure.
-- src:342 | (3) If an individual opts out, in the manner determined by the
-- src:343 | Commissioner, from the application of subsection (1) to means
-- src:344 | information about the individual, then from the time an authorised
-- src:345 | person is notified that the individual has opted out, the authorised
-- src:346 | person must not —
-- src:354 | (b) use or disclose under section 9 any such means information
-- src:355 | that the authorised person had previously accessed,
-- src:357 | except with the consent of that individual.
@ref SSSA2015 s 8(3)(b) (src:342-357)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party under the Act` `An act under the Act`
`s 8(3)(b) bar on the authorised person` MEANS
    PARTY `the authorised person`
    SHANT `use or disclose the means information`
    LEST BREACH BY `the authorised person` BECAUSE "the authorised person used or disclosed means information after being notified that the individual opted out, and without the individual's consent"

-- EXPECT BREACH: the authorised person accesses at time 3 (BREACH BY the authorised person).
#TRACE `s 8(3)(a) bar on the authorised person` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the authorised person` DOES `access the means information` AT 3
-- EXPECT PENDING: nothing done by time 100; the bar is still running (MUST NOT access), not fulfilled and not breached.
#TRACE `s 8(3)(a) bar on the authorised person` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)
-- EXPECT BREACH: the authorised person uses or discloses at time 3 (BREACH BY the authorised person).
#TRACE `s 8(3)(b) bar on the authorised person` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the authorised person` DOES `use or disclose the means information` AT 3

-- s 8(4)(a): "a person is not guilty of an offence under any written law or of any
-- breach of confidence, and does not incur any other civil liability, by virtue
-- merely of the person disclosing any information in accordance with any
-- direction".  It is "subject to subsection (3)": where s 8(3) bars the act, or
-- that is not known, the immunity is not answered.
-- src:359 | (4) Despite the provisions of this Act or any other written law, but
-- src:360 | subject to subsection (3) —
-- src:362 | (a) a person is not guilty of an offence under any written law or
-- src:363 | of any breach of confidence, and does not incur any other
-- src:364 | civil liability, by virtue merely of the person disclosing any
-- src:365 | information in accordance with any direction under
-- src:366 | subsection (1)(a) or (2)(a);
@ref SSSA2015 s 8(4)(a) (src:359-366)
GIVEN `the person discloses information in accordance with a direction under section 8(1)(a) or 8(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 8(3) bars the act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(4)(a) the person is not guilty or liable merely by disclosing in accordance with the direction` MEANS
    IF `the person discloses information in accordance with a direction under section 8(1)(a) or 8(2)(a)`
       AND (`section 8(3) bars the act` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the immunity is "by virtue merely of the person disclosing any information in accordance with any direction" and is "subject to subsection (3)"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 8(4)(b): an authorised person who is an officer of an information recipient,
-- acting in good faith and with reasonable care, accessing or disclosing to another
-- authorised person who is an officer of the same recipient means information
-- obtained under s 8(1) in the performance of duties connected with the
-- administration or enforcement of the Act or the administration of the Scheme.
-- src:359 | (4) Despite the provisions of this Act or any other written law, but
-- src:360 | subject to subsection (3) —
-- src:368 | (b) an authorised person (being an officer of an information
-- src:369 | recipient) is not guilty of an offence under any written law
-- src:370 | or of any breach of confidence, and does not incur any
-- src:371 | other civil liability, by virtue merely of the authorised
-- src:372 | person (acting in good faith and with reasonable care)
-- src:373 | accessing, or disclosing to another authorised person
-- src:374 | (being an officer of the same information recipient), any
-- src:375 | means information obtained under subsection (1) in the
-- src:376 | performance of the authorised person’s duties connected
-- src:377 | with the administration or enforcement of this Act or the
-- src:378 | administration of the Scheme; and
@ref SSSA2015 s 8(4)(b) (src:359-378)
GIVEN conduct IS A `Conduct of an officer of an information recipient`
      `section 8(3) bars the act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(4)(b) the authorised person is not guilty or liable merely by accessing or disclosing the means information` MEANS
    IF conduct's `is an officer of an information recipient`
       AND conduct's `is an authorised person`
       AND conduct's `acts in good faith`
       AND conduct's `acts with reasonable care`
       AND (conduct's `accesses the information` OR (conduct's `discloses the information to another officer of the same information recipient` AND conduct's `that other officer is an authorised person`))
       AND conduct's `the information is means information obtained under section 8(1)`
       AND conduct's `the conduct is in the performance of duties connected with the administration or enforcement of this Act or the administration of the Scheme`
       AND (`section 8(3) bars the act` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the immunity is "by virtue merely of" the access or disclosure described, "acting in good faith and with reasonable care", and is "subject to subsection (3)"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 8(4)(c): the same for an officer of an information recipient and confidential information obtained under s 8(2).
-- src:359 | (4) Despite the provisions of this Act or any other written law, but
-- src:360 | subject to subsection (3) —
-- src:380 | (c) an officer of an information recipient is not guilty of an
-- src:381 | offence under any written law or of any breach of
-- src:382 | confidence, and does not incur any other civil liability,
-- src:383 | by virtue merely of the officer (acting in good faith and
-- src:384 | with reasonable care) accessing, or disclosing to another
-- src:385 | officer of the same information recipient, any confidential
-- src:386 | information obtained under subsection (2) in the
-- src:387 | performance of the officer’s duties connected with the
-- src:388 | administration or enforcement of this Act or the
-- src:389 | administration of the Scheme.
@ref SSSA2015 s 8(4)(c) (src:359-389)
GIVEN conduct IS A `Conduct of an officer of an information recipient`
      `section 8(3) bars the act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(4)(c) the officer is not guilty or liable merely by accessing or disclosing the confidential information` MEANS
    IF conduct's `is an officer of an information recipient`
       AND conduct's `acts in good faith`
       AND conduct's `acts with reasonable care`
       AND (conduct's `accesses the information` OR conduct's `discloses the information to another officer of the same information recipient`)
       AND conduct's `the information is confidential information other than means information obtained under section 8(2)`
       AND conduct's `the conduct is in the performance of duties connected with the administration or enforcement of this Act or the administration of the Scheme`
       AND (`section 8(3) bars the act` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the immunity is "by virtue merely of" the access or disclosure described, "acting in good faith and with reasonable care", and is "subject to subsection (3)"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 8(5): "may be given on such terms and conditions ... as the Minister giving the direction considers appropriate".
-- src:391 | (5) A direction under subsection (1)(a) or (2)(a) may be given on
