`s 8(6) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the act is in contravention of section 8(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is "any act in contravention of subsection (3)", and the subsection says nothing of any other act
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:400 | (6) Any person who does any act in contravention of subsection (3)
-- src:401 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:402 | not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:403 | 12 months or to both.
@ref SSSA2015 s 8(6) (src:400-403)
GIVEN fine IS A NUMBER
      months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(6) the sentence is within the greatest penalty` MEANS
    IF `a sentence is within the ceiling of a penalty` (`s 8(6) the greatest penalty`) fine months
