-- s 8(7) "information recipient" means the Commissioner, the Board or an administrator.
-- src:415 | “information recipient” means the Commissioner, the Board or
-- src:416 | an administrator;
@ref SSSA2015 s 8(7) "information recipient" (src:415-416)
GIVEN capacity IS A Capacity
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(7) the person is an information recipient` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF capacity EQUALS `the Commissioner for Silver Support`
           OR capacity EQUALS `a Deputy Commissioner for Silver Support`
           OR capacity EQUALS `an Assistant Commissioner for Silver Support`
           OR capacity EQUALS `the Board`
           OR capacity EQUALS `an administrator who is a public officer`
           OR capacity EQUALS `an administrator that is a public authority other than the Board`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“information recipient” means the Commissioner, the Board or an administrator"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 8(7) "authorised person" means (a) the Commissioner, or (b) any other officer of an information recipient authorised by the Minister to have access to means information obtained under s 8(1).
-- src:407 | “authorised person” means —
-- src:409 | (a) the Commissioner; or
-- src:411 | (b) any other officer of an information recipient who is
-- src:412 | authorised by the Minister to have access to means
-- src:413 | information obtained under subsection (1);
@ref SSSA2015 s 8(7) "authorised person" (src:407-413)
GIVEN appointment IS AN `Appointment under section 4`
      `the person is an officer of an information recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorised by the Minister to have access to means information obtained under section 8(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(7) the person is an authorised person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 the person is the Commissioner` appointment EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is an officer of an information recipient` AND `the person is authorised by the Minister to have access to means information obtained under section 8(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“authorised person” means — (a) the Commissioner; or (b) any other officer of an information recipient who is authorised by the Minister"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 8(7) "officer", in relation to an information recipient: five cases, one per kind of recipient.
-- Each case names who is an officer; anyone else is not (a definition that "means").
-- src:418 | “officer”, in relation to an information recipient, means —
-- src:420 | (a) in any case where the information recipient is a
-- src:421 | Commissioner who is a public officer, the
-- src:422 | Commissioner or any public officer acting under
-- src:423 | the Commissioner’s direction;
-- src:425 | (b) in any case where the information recipient is a
-- src:426 | Commissioner who is an employee of a public
-- src:427 | authority, the Commissioner or any employee of
-- src:428 | the same public authority acting under the
-- src:429 | Commissioner’s direction;
-- src:431 | (c) in any case where the information recipient is the
-- src:432 | Board, any member, officer or employee of the
-- src:433 | Board;
-- src:435 | (d) in any case where the information recipient is an
-- src:436 | administrator who is a public officer, the
-- src:437 | administrator and any public officer acting under
-- src:438 | the administrator’s direction; and
-- src:440 | (e) in any case where the information recipient is an
-- src:441 | administrator which is a public authority (other than
-- src:446 | the Board), any member, officer or employee of the
-- src:447 | administrator.
@ref SSSA2015 s 8(7) "officer" (src:418-447)
GIVEN recipient IS AN `Information recipient asked about`
      relation IS A `Relation to the information recipient`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(7) the person is an officer in relation to the information recipient` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF recipient EQUALS `a Commissioner who is a public officer`
           AND (relation EQUALS `the recipient itself` OR relation EQUALS `a public officer acting under the recipient's direction`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF recipient EQUALS `a Commissioner who is an employee of a public authority`
           AND (relation EQUALS `the recipient itself` OR relation EQUALS `an employee of the same public authority acting under the Commissioner's direction`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF recipient EQUALS `the Board as recipient`
           AND relation EQUALS `a member, officer or employee of the Board`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF recipient EQUALS `an administrator who is a public officer as recipient`
           AND (relation EQUALS `the recipient itself` OR relation EQUALS `a public officer acting under the recipient's direction`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF recipient EQUALS `an administrator that is a public authority other than the Board as recipient`
           AND relation EQUALS `a member, officer or employee of the administrator`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“officer”, in relation to an information recipient, means"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 9 Use of information`

-- s 9(1): this section applies to the persons it lists.  The list is not closed
-- with "only", so a person it does not list is not answered.
-- src:451 | 9.—(1) This section applies to the Commissioner, the Board, an
-- src:452 | administrator, any public officer (or employee of a public authority)
-- src:453 | acting under the Commissioner’s direction, any public officer acting
-- src:454 | under the direction of an administrator (being a public officer), and
-- src:455 | any member, officer or employee of the Board or of an administrator
-- src:456 | (being a public authority other than the Board).
@ref SSSA2015 s 9(1) (src:451-456)
GIVEN capacity IS A Capacity
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(1) section 9 applies to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF capacity EQUALS `the Commissioner for Silver Support`
           OR capacity EQUALS `a Deputy Commissioner for Silver Support`
           OR capacity EQUALS `an Assistant Commissioner for Silver Support`
           OR capacity EQUALS `the Board`
           OR capacity EQUALS `an administrator who is a public officer`
           OR capacity EQUALS `an administrator that is a public authority other than the Board`
           OR capacity EQUALS `a public officer or employee of a public authority acting under the Commissioner's direction`
           OR capacity EQUALS `a public officer acting under the direction of an administrator who is a public officer`
           OR capacity EQUALS `a member, officer or employee of the Board`
           OR capacity EQUALS `a member, officer or employee of an administrator that is a public authority other than the Board`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the section "applies to" the persons listed and does not say it applies to no one else
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 9(2): the purpose test.  "authorised only if the purpose ... is to communicate or manage the information as part of (a) the administration or enforcement of this Act; or (b) the administration of the Scheme".
-- src:458 | (2) The use or disclosure of means information obtained under
-- src:459 | section 8(1), or of confidential information (other than means
-- src:460 | information) obtained under section 8(2), without the consent of
-- src:461 | the individual to whom the information relates, is authorised only if
-- src:462 | the purpose of the use or disclosure is to communicate or manage the
-- src:463 | information as part of —
-- src:465 | (a) the administration or enforcement of this Act; or
-- src:467 | (b) the administration of the Scheme.
@ref SSSA2015 s 9(2) (src:458-467)
GIVEN use IS A `Use or disclosure asked about under section 9(2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(2) the purpose is one the subsection names` MEANS
    use's `has the purpose of communicating or managing the information as part of the administration or enforcement of this Act`
    OR use's `has the purpose of communicating or managing the information as part of the administration of the Scheme`

-- src:458 | (2) The use or disclosure of means information obtained under
-- src:459 | section 8(1), or of confidential information (other than means
-- src:460 | information) obtained under section 8(2), without the consent of
-- src:461 | the individual to whom the information relates, is authorised only if
-- src:462 | the purpose of the use or disclosure is to communicate or manage the
-- src:463 | information as part of —
-- src:465 | (a) the administration or enforcement of this Act; or
-- src:467 | (b) the administration of the Scheme.
@ref SSSA2015 s 9(2) (src:458-467)
GIVEN use IS A `Use or disclosure asked about under section 9(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(2) the use or disclosure is authorised` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT use's `is of means information obtained under section 8(1) or of confidential information other than means information obtained under section 8(2)`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of "means information obtained under section 8(1)" and "confidential information (other than means information) obtained under section 8(2)"
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT use's `is without the consent of the individual to whom the information relates`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of a use or disclosure "without the consent of the individual to whom the information relates"
        THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is authorised only if the purpose of the use or disclosure is to communicate or manage the information as part of"
        IF NOT (`s 9(2) the purpose is one the subsection names` use) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "only if" states a condition that must be met and does not say the use or disclosure is authorised once it is met
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 9(3): the Commissioner, the Board or an administrator may provide derived
-- information for a prescribed public scheme "only at the request of" the
-- recipient "and with the approval of the Minister" and "only in the form of a
-- report stating" both (i) and (ii).  Which public schemes are prescribed is in
-- regulations that are not among the sources, so it is an input.  A failed "only"
-- limb answers no whether or not the scheme is known to be prescribed.
-- src:469 | (3) Despite subsection (2), the Commissioner, the Board or an
-- src:470 | administrator may provide information derived from means
-- src:471 | information obtained under section 8(1), or from confidential
-- src:472 | information (other than means information) obtained under
-- src:473 | section 8(2), to a public officer, a public authority or any other
-- src:474 | person or organisation, for the development or implementation of any
-- src:475 | public scheme that may be prescribed for the purposes of this
-- src:476 | subsection —
-- src:478 | (a) only at the request of the public officer, public authority,
-- src:479 | person or organisation (as the case may be) and with the
-- src:480 | approval of the Minister; and
-- src:482 | (b) only in the form of a report stating —
-- src:484 | (i) whether an individual satisfies the eligibility criteria
-- src:485 | for receiving any benefit under the Scheme; and
-- src:487 | (ii) the description and amount of each benefit that the
-- src:488 | individual is eligible to receive or has received under
-- src:493 | the Scheme up to the date on which the report is
-- src:494 | made.
@ref SSSA2015 s 9(3) (src:469-494)
GIVEN provider IS A Capacity
      `the information is derived from means information obtained under section 8(1), or from confidential information other than means information obtained under section 8(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is for the development or implementation of a public scheme prescribed for the purposes of section 9(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the information is provided at the request of the public officer, public authority, person or organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has approved the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is provided in the form of a report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states whether the individual satisfies the eligibility criteria for receiving any benefit under the Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states the description and amount of each benefit that the individual is eligible to receive or has received under the Scheme up to the date of the report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(3) the Commissioner, the Board or an administrator may provide the information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 8(7) the person is an information recipient` provider EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the permission is given to "the Commissioner, the Board or an administrator"
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT `the information is derived from means information obtained under section 8(1), or from confidential information other than means information obtained under section 8(2)`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the permission is for "information derived from means information obtained under section 8(1), or from confidential information"
        THEN NOTHING
        IF `the information is for the development or implementation of a public scheme prescribed for the purposes of section 9(3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the permission is "for the development or implementation of any public scheme that may be prescribed for the purposes of this subsection"
        THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only at the request of the public officer, public authority, person or organisation (as the case may be)"
        IF NOT `the information is provided at the request of the public officer, public authority, person or organisation` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "with the approval of the Minister"
        IF NOT `the Minister has approved the provision` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only in the form of a report stating"
        IF NOT `the information is provided in the form of a report` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "whether an individual satisfies the eligibility criteria for receiving any benefit under the Scheme"
        IF NOT `the report states whether the individual satisfies the eligibility criteria for receiving any benefit under the Scheme` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the description and amount of each benefit that the individual is eligible to receive or has received under"
        IF NOT `the report states the description and amount of each benefit that the individual is eligible to receive or has received under the Scheme up to the date of the report` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): which public scheme "may be prescribed for the purposes of this subsection" is in regulations that are not among the sources
        IF `the information is for the development or implementation of a public scheme prescribed for the purposes of section 9(3)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 9(4): "An approval under subsection (3)(a) may be given on such terms and conditions ... as the Minister considers appropriate."
-- src:496 | (4) An approval under subsection (3)(a) may be given on such
-- src:497 | terms and conditions (regarding access to the information provided
-- src:498 | pursuant to the approval) as the Minister considers appropriate.
@ref SSSA2015 s 9(4) (src:496-498)
GIVEN `the approval is an approval under section 9(3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(4) the Minister may give the approval on terms and conditions regarding access` MEANS
    IF `the approval is an approval under section 9(3)(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "An approval under subsection (3)(a)"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 9(5): an individual who has opted out of the report.  Shaped like s 8(3): the
-- "If" gives no when it fails (reading (a)), "from the time ... is notified" is a
-- start time (reading (b)), and "except with the consent of the individual" gives no.
-- src:500 | (5) If an individual opts out, in the manner determined by the
-- src:501 | Commissioner, from the provision of a report about the individual
-- src:502 | mentioned in subsection (3)(b), then from the time the Commissioner,
-- src:503 | the Board or an administrator is notified that the individual has opted
-- src:504 | out, except with the consent of the individual, the Commissioner, the
-- src:505 | Board or the administrator (as the case may be) must not provide any
-- src:506 | such report about the individual.
@ref SSSA2015 s 9(5) (src:500-506)
GIVEN provider IS A Capacity
      `the report is a report about the individual mentioned in section 9(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has opted out, in the manner determined by the Commissioner, from the provision of the report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner, the Board or the administrator has been notified that the individual has opted out` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(5) the provider is barred from providing the report` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 8(7) the person is an information recipient` provider EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on "the Commissioner, the Board or the administrator (as the case may be)"
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT `the report is a report about the individual mentioned in section 9(3)(b)`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on providing "any such report about the individual"
        THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an individual opts out, in the manner determined by the Commissioner, from the provision of a report"
        IF NOT `the individual has opted out, in the manner determined by the Commissioner, from the provision of the report` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except with the consent of the individual"
        IF `the individual has consented` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar runs "from the time the Commissioner, the Board or an administrator is notified that the individual has opted out"
        IF NOT `the Commissioner, the Board or the administrator has been notified that the individual has opted out` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The same bar as a regulative rule.
-- src:500 | (5) If an individual opts out, in the manner determined by the
-- src:501 | Commissioner, from the provision of a report about the individual
-- src:502 | mentioned in subsection (3)(b), then from the time the Commissioner,
-- src:503 | the Board or an administrator is notified that the individual has opted
-- src:504 | out, except with the consent of the individual, the Commissioner, the
-- src:505 | Board or the administrator (as the case may be) must not provide any
-- src:506 | such report about the individual.
@ref SSSA2015 s 9(5) (src:500-506)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party under the Act` `An act under the Act`
`s 9(5) bar on the Commissioner, the Board or the administrator` MEANS
    PARTY `the Commissioner, the Board or the administrator`
    SHANT `provide a report about the individual`
    LEST BREACH BY `the Commissioner, the Board or the administrator` BECAUSE "the Commissioner, the Board or the administrator provided a report about an individual who had opted out, without the individual's consent"

-- EXPECT BREACH: the provider provides a report at time 3 (BREACH BY the Commissioner, the Board or the administrator).
#TRACE `s 9(5) bar on the Commissioner, the Board or the administrator` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner, the Board or the administrator` DOES `provide a report about the individual` AT 3
-- EXPECT PENDING: nothing done by time 100; the bar is still running, not breached.
#TRACE `s 9(5) bar on the Commissioner, the Board or the administrator` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

-- s 9(6): the Board may use, to administer the Scheme, so much of the means
-- information and other confidential information obtained in the course of its
-- duties under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953 as the Minister approves.  The
-- text says "(whether before, on or after 18 January 2016)", so the date on which
-- the Board obtained the information makes no difference and is not an input.
-- src:508 | (6) The Board may use to administer the Scheme so much of the
-- src:509 | means information and other confidential information obtained by the
-- src:510 | Board (whether before, on or after 18 January 2016) in the course of
-- src:511 | performing the Board’s duties under the Central Provident Fund
-- src:512 | Act 1953 as the Minister approves to be used for such purpose.
@ref SSSA2015 s 9(6) (src:508-512)
GIVEN user IS A Capacity
      `the information was obtained by the Board in the course of performing the Board's duties under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has approved the use for the purpose of administering the Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(6) the Board may use the information to administer the Scheme` MEANS
    IF user EQUALS `the Board`
       AND `the information was obtained by the Board in the course of performing the Board's duties under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953`
       AND `the Minister has approved the use for the purpose of administering the Scheme`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the permission is the Board's, over "so much of" the information "as the Minister approves to be used for such purpose"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 9(7): the offence of contravening s 9(2), (3) or (5).  The three results are
-- those of the functions above: a use or disclosure that s 9(2) does not authorise,
-- a provision that s 9(3) does not permit, or a report that s 9(5) bars.
-- fields:                                 greatest fine in dollars, greatest imprisonment in months
-- src:514 | (7) Any person who does any act in contravention of subsection (2),
-- src:515 | (3) or (5) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- src:516 | to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:517 | exceeding 12 months or to both.
@ref SSSA2015 s 9(7) (src:514-517)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 9(7) the greatest penalty` MEANS Penalty OF 5000, 12

-- src:514 | (7) Any person who does any act in contravention of subsection (2),
-- src:515 | (3) or (5) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- src:516 | to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:517 | exceeding 12 months or to both.
@ref SSSA2015 s 9(7) (src:514-517)
GIVEN `the act contravenes section 9(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the act contravenes section 9(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the act contravenes section 9(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(7) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the act contravenes section 9(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the act contravenes section 9(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the act contravenes section 9(5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is "any act in contravention of subsection (2), (3) or (5)", and the subsection says nothing of any other act
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:514 | (7) Any person who does any act in contravention of subsection (2),
-- src:515 | (3) or (5) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- src:516 | to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:517 | exceeding 12 months or to both.
@ref SSSA2015 s 9(7) (src:514-517)
GIVEN fine IS A NUMBER
      months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(7) the sentence is within the greatest penalty` MEANS
    IF `a sentence is within the ceiling of a penalty` (`s 9(7) the greatest penalty`) fine months
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 10 Recovery of sums overpaid, etc.`

-- s 10(1): where a benefit is paid as a cash grant, the whole amount is recoverable
-- if the recipient is not an eligible individual (a)(i) or is not eligible for that
-- grant (a)(ii), and the excess if the amount paid is more than the recipient is
-- eligible to receive (b).  The answer is the amount made recoverable by this
-- subsection; nil (JUST 0) is the text's own no, "If" having failed (reading (a)).
-- An unknown answers NOTHING only when the answer turns on it.  A recipient known
-- not to be eligible for that cash grant owes the amount paid whether or not the
-- recipient is an eligible individual: by (a)(i) if not, by (a)(ii) if so.
-- src:521 | 10.—(1) If any benefit under the Scheme is disbursed as a cash
-- src:522 | grant, and —
-- src:524 | (a) the recipient —
-- src:526 | (i) is not an eligible individual; or
-- src:528 | (ii) is an eligible individual, but is not eligible for that
-- src:529 | cash grant; or
-- src:531 | (b) the amount paid is in excess of the amount the recipient is
-- src:532 | eligible to receive by way of that cash grant,
-- src:534 | the amount paid or paid in excess (as the case may be) is recoverable
-- src:535 | from the recipient as a debt due to the Government.
@ref SSSA2015 s 10(1) (src:521-535)
GIVEN `the benefit is disbursed as a cash grant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recipient is an eligible individual` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the recipient is eligible for that cash grant` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount the recipient is eligible to receive by way of that cash grant` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 10(1) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- nil (FALSE-kind: the text says no in its own words): "If any benefit under the Scheme is disbursed as a cash grant"
        IF NOT `the benefit is disbursed as a cash grant` THEN JUST 0
        -- (a)(i): the recipient is not an eligible individual -- the amount paid
        IF `the recipient is an eligible individual` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST `the amount paid`
        -- (a)(ii), and (a)(i) when it is not known whether the recipient is an eligible individual: a recipient who is not eligible for that cash grant either "is not an eligible individual" (a)(i) or "is an eligible individual, but is not eligible for that cash grant" (a)(ii), and "the amount paid" is recoverable under each, so the status is not needed -- the amount paid
        -- (this arm stands ahead of the arm for an unknown status on purpose: an unknown status must not block an answer that does not need it)
        IF `the recipient is eligible for that cash grant` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST `the amount paid`
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the recipient is an eligible individual turns on criteria that may be prescribed
        IF `the recipient is an eligible individual` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): what the recipient is eligible for turns on benefits and amounts that may be prescribed
        IF `the recipient is eligible for that cash grant` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- (b): the excess, if any
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the amount the recipient is eligible to receive by way of that cash grant`
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the amount the recipient is eligible to receive is prescribed
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST eligibleAmount THEN
                IF `the amount paid` GREATER THAN eligibleAmount
                THEN JUST (`the amount paid` MINUS eligibleAmount)
                -- nil (FALSE-kind: the text says no in its own words): "the amount paid is in excess of the amount the recipient is eligible to receive"
                ELSE JUST 0

-- s 10(2): an individual (eligible or not) who obtains a cash grant or other
-- benefit by a false or misleading statement made knowingly or recklessly, or by a
-- document the individual knows, or ought reasonably to know, is false in a
-- material particular: the amount so obtained is recoverable.
-- src:540 | (2) If any individual (whether or not an eligible individual) obtains
-- src:541 | any cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme —
-- src:543 | (a) by knowingly or recklessly making any false or misleading
-- src:544 | statement; or
-- src:546 | (b) by producing or providing, or causing to be produced or
-- src:547 | provided, any document which the individual knows, or
-- src:548 | ought reasonably to know, is false in a material particular,
-- src:550 | the amount of the cash grant or other benefit so obtained is
-- src:551 | recoverable from the individual as a debt due to the Government.
@ref SSSA2015 s 10(2) (src:540-551)
GIVEN `the individual obtained a cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme by knowingly or recklessly making a false or misleading statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual obtained a cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme by producing or providing, or causing to be produced or provided, a document which the individual knows, or ought reasonably to know, is false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the cash grant or other benefit so obtained` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 10(2) the amount made recoverable as a debt due to the Government` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the individual obtained a cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme by knowingly or recklessly making a false or misleading statement`
           OR `the individual obtained a cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme by producing or providing, or causing to be produced or provided, a document which the individual knows, or ought reasonably to know, is false in a material particular`
        THEN `the amount of the cash grant or other benefit so obtained`
        -- nil (FALSE-kind: the text says no in its own words): "If any individual (whether or not an eligible individual) obtains any cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme"
        OTHERWISE 0

-- s 10(3): an administrator may recover the amount due under (1) or (2) from a cash
-- grant or other benefit the person is eligible to receive, and from any other sum
-- payable to the person by the administrator.  The two sources are listed without
-- "only", so another source is not answered.
-- src:553 | (3) An administrator may recover on behalf of the Government the
-- src:554 | amount due to the Government under subsection (1) or (2), by set‑off
-- src:555 | or otherwise, from —
-- src:557 | (a) any cash grant or other benefit which the recipient in
-- src:558 | subsection (1) or individual in subsection (2) (as the case
-- src:559 | may be) is eligible to receive under the Scheme; and
-- src:561 | (b) any other sum that is payable to that recipient or individual
-- src:562 | by the administrator.
@ref SSSA2015 s 10(3) (src:553-562)
GIVEN `the person recovering is an administrator` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an amount is due to the Government under section 10(1) or 10(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      source IS A `Source of recovery`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(3) the administrator may recover the amount from the source` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person recovering is an administrator` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "An administrator"'s
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT `an amount is due to the Government under section 10(1) or 10(2)`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to recover "the amount due to the Government under subsection (1) or (2)"
        THEN NOTHING
        IF source EQUALS `a cash grant or other benefit the recipient is eligible to receive under the Scheme` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF source EQUALS `another sum payable to the recipient by the administrator` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sources are listed as "(a)" and "(b)" without "only", and the power is "by set‑off or otherwise"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
